WARNING:ENOSYS: ENOSYS means 'invalid syscall nr' and nothing else
#718: FILE: drivers/gpio/sx150x.c:643:
+		return -ENOSYS;

ENOSYS means that a nonexistent system call was called.
Earlier, it was wrongly used for things like invalid operations on
otherwise valid syscalls.  This should be avoided in new code.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/5eb299021dec23c1a48fa7d9f2c8b794e967766d.1408730669.git.luto@amacapital.net/

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*chip)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct sx150x_chip)...)
#720: FILE: drivers/gpio/sx150x.c:645:
+	chip = kzalloc(sizeof(struct sx150x_chip), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

